sentences.l:
there to him Eurypylus, struck, came face to face,
Zeus-sprung Euaemon’s-son, in the thigh with an arrow,
limping from the war;

and down ran wet sweat
from his shoulders and head, and from the wound, grievous,
dark blood gurgled;

sentences.t:
ἀλλ’ ἄγε μοι τόδε εἰπὲ διοτρεφὲς Εὐρύπυλ’ ἥρως,
ἤ ῥ’ ἔτι που σχήσουσι πελώριον Ἕκτορ’ Ἀχαιοί,
ἦ ἤδη φθίσονται ὑπ’ αὐτοῦ δουρὶ δαμέντες;

sentences.tr:
all’ age moi tode eipe diotrephes Eurypyl’ hērōs,
ē rh’ eti pou schēsousi pelōrion Hektor’ Achaioi,
ē ēdē phthisontai hyp’ autou douri damentes;

sentences.l:
For those indeed, all, who before were the best,
among the ships lie, struck and wounded
under the hands of the Trojans;
